# .notes

Daily notes + YouTrack / GitLab for Sublime Text 4.

Knowledge base lives in the separate **kb** package (palette **`.kb`**). Overlap is only `kb:topic/subject` insert + hover.

- **Package folder / Package Control name:** `notes`
- **Command Palette:** type **`.notes`** (same pattern as **`.kubetools`**)
- **Syntax name:** Notes (follows your active color scheme — dark and light)
- **Settings file:** `ST4Notes.sublime-settings` (User path kept so existing tokens keep working)

Stores a single plain-text notes file with commands to add/search entries, open tickets, import issues, optionally post YouTrack comments, hover GitLab MRs, and insert `kb:` refs (knowledge base is the **kb** package).

## Commands (Cmd+Shift+P / Ctrl+Shift+P — type `.notes`)

| Command | What it does |
|---------|----------------|
| **.notes - Hub** | Getting started / weekly summary / weekly search |
| **.notes - Add** | Today's headers (append) / **New note** / YouTrack import / **Issue** |
| **.notes - View** | Read-only journal. **Alt+Up/Down** selects a `# HEADER:`. **Enter** opens a note slice (commit **replaces** that day's block). |
| **.notes - Search** | Quick-panel search over tickets / TODO / OPS |
| **.notes - Search Recently Resolved** | YouTrack: my resolved/closed issues (newest updated first) |
| **.notes - Open Issue** | All issues → pick assignee → palette list (type to filter live, Enter opens) |
| **.notes - Settings** | Edit package settings |

## Notes: Add and edit

The journal is a list of **headers** (`# PROJ-1234:`, `# TODO:`, `# standup:`) under a date. The file is read-only in **.notes - View**; all edits go through a slice.

### Edit today's (or that day's) block

1. **.notes - View**
2. **Alt+Up / Alt+Down** until the header is selected
3. **Enter** — slice opens with that day's bullets
4. Edit freely. **Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+Enter** **replaces** that header's block on that calendar day. Close the tab to cancel.

Enter on empty space (not inside a header) opens an empty **New note** slice (appends under today).

### Add a new header

**.notes - Add** → **New note** → set **`topic:`** to any label (`PROJ-99`, `TODO`, `standup`, `weekly standup`) → bullets → commit. Creates `# topic:` under today if missing, then appends. This is a journal heading, not a YouTrack id. YouTrack comments are **not** posted from New note (even if `post_comments` is on). Pick the ticket from Add’s list (or Import) to append *and* comment.

`PROJ-1234` and `proj-1234` are the same heading. `proj 1234` and `proj_1234` are different headings and will not merge.

### Append to an existing header today

**.notes - Add** → pick a header already on today → slice with empty body → commit **appends** bullets (does not rewrite older lines).

### YouTrack issue (not a journal edit)

**.notes - Add** → **Issue** or import — still the YouTrack issue slice.

Example result:

```
# PROJ-1234:
- first line
- second line
- [DONE]<<-
```

No `[HH:MM]` timestamps are added (legacy timestamps in old notes still highlight).

## Hover

- **YouTrack** issue URL / ticket id → summary, state, assignee, …  
- **GitLab MR** URL (`…/-/merge_requests/N`) → popup header shows `!N` (click opens the MR); status, pipeline, changed files (requires `gitlab_base` + `gitlab_token`)
  - Click a changed file → browser opens the MR **Changes** tab focused on that file (`#diff-content-{sha1(path)}`)

## Settings

Preferences → Package Settings → **notes** (keep tokens in **User** settings only).
Settings resource filename remains `ST4Notes.sublime-settings` for compatibility with
`Packages/User/ST4Notes.sublime-settings`.

| Key | Notes |
|-----|--------|
| `notes_file` | Default `~/Documents/ST4Notes` |
| `knowledge_base_file` | Default `~/Documents/ST4Notes-kb` — used by **kb** until `User/KB.sublime-settings` exists |
| `youtrack_base` / `youtrack_token` | YouTrack |
| `gitlab_base` / `gitlab_token` | GitLab MR hover (`read_api`) |
| `default_project` | YouTrack project shortName (e.g. `MYPROJECT`) |
| `issue_stages` | Sub-task **labels** that seed Create Issue (e.g. `Design,Dev,QA,Deploy` or env names). Empty uses those four in the slice; commit with `stages: true` saves the labels back here. |
| `notes_path_jail` | `notes_file` must stay under this dir (default `~`) |
| `note_max_lines` / `note_max_line_len` | Multi-line Add limits (50 / 500) |
| `post_comments` | Default `false` |
| `notes_seed_demo` | Seed starter examples when the journal file is missing or empty |
| `show_getting_started` | Open the getting-started tab once after install (opt out with `false`) |
| `kb_hover_enabled` / `kb_popup_*` / `kb_seed_demo` / `kb_git_friendly` | Legacy keys; prefer **kb** / `KB.sublime-settings` |

## Issue slice (YouTrack)

**.notes - Add** → **Issue** (empty) or import from YouTrack. Same slice either way.

**Commit:** **Cmd+Shift+Enter** (Mac) / **Ctrl+Shift+Enter** (Win/Linux). Close the tab to cancel.

- New issue: `ticket:` is read-only (YouTrack assigns the id on commit). `description:` is multiline — indent extra lines with two spaces.
- Import: `ticket:` is filled and locked; other fields are populated from YouTrack. Body bullets below `---` become a journal note.

Contract: **fields above `---`**, **body below**.

### Fields (above `---`)

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `ticket` | Read-only. Empty on create; import fills `PROJ-1234`. |
| `project` | YouTrack shortName. Required when creating a **new** parent. |
| `summary` | Parent title. Also fills `$summary` and `$name` in sub-task titles. |
| `description` | Issue description (multiline; indent continuation lines). |
| `assignee` | YouTrack **email** (prefills yours on create) or login. Empty = unassigned. |
| `reporter` / `due` / `state` / `priority` | Filled on import (informational). |
| `parent` | Empty = create a new parent from `summary`. Or `PROJ-1234` / issue URL to attach children only. |
| `stages` | `true` = create the sub-tasks listed below. `false` (default) = a single issue from `summary`. |

### Sub-tickets (below `---`, when `stages: true`)

One child per line:

```text
- <label> | <title template>
```

- **Left of `|`** is the label (`$stage`). It is saved to `issue_stages` on commit.
- **Right of `|`** is the YouTrack title. Placeholders:
  - `$summary` / `$name` → parent `summary`
  - `$stage` → the label on that line
- Delete a line to skip that child. Ignored when `stages: false`.

Default lines (from `issue_stages`, or Design / Dev / QA / Deploy if empty):

```text
- Design | $name - Design
- Dev | $name - Dev
- QA | $name - QA
- Deploy | $name - Deploy
```

**Override `$name` with env names** (instead of Design/Dev):

```text
summary: Roll out sealed-secrets docs
stages: true
---
- env-dev | $name - env-dev
- env-test | $name - env-test
```

Creates parent `Roll out sealed-secrets docs` plus children titled `Roll out sealed-secrets docs - env-dev` and `… - env-test`. Same idea with `$summary - $stage`.

Attach **only sub-tasks** under an existing ticket (`summary` can stay empty — title is fetched for `$name`):

```text
parent: PROJ-1234
stages: true
---
- env-dev | $name - env-dev
- env-test | $name - env-test
```

## Knowledge base (package **kb**)

Install **kb** and use Command Palette **`.kb`**. Notes only inserts/hovers `kb:topic/subject`.

Single file (`knowledge_base_file`) with topics and subjects:

```text
# TOPIC: my-topic
## SUBJECT: my-subject
command examples and notes…

## SUBJECT: another
…
```

| Action | How |
|--------|-----|
| Hub | `.kb - Hub` |
| Browse | topics → subjects; arrows preview in KB file; Enter opens **edit-slice** (Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+Enter saves) |
| Search | flat subject list; same arrow-preview / Enter behavior |
| Create subject | `.kb - Create Subject` (or hub) → **edit-slice** only (nothing written until commit). SUBJECT selected; pick topic with **Cmd/Ctrl+Alt+T**. Closing the tab without commit leaves no stub in the KB file. |
| Move subject | Hub **Move subject to topic…** → pick subject → pick topic (or New topic…). Writes immediately; empty source topics are dropped. |
| Slice keys | **Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+Enter** commit · **Cmd/Ctrl+Alt+T** topic picker (then SUBJECT is selected) · **Alt+Up / Alt+Down** next/prev field (not created date) · **Cmd/Ctrl+Alt+B** code fence |
| KB file | Read-only in Sublime. **Alt+Up / Alt+Down** jumps **SUBJECT** titles. Change content via edit-slice only. Slice commit (and hub **Format knowledge base**) rewrites **canonical layout**: one blank line between subjects, two before each later `# TOPIC:`, headers `## SUBJECT` / `- created` / `- modified`, LF, no reorder, dates unchanged by format. |
| Insert ref | `.kb - Insert Ref` → `kb:topic/subject` at caret |
| Hover ref | topic → subjects panel; subject title or `kb:…` line → **edit-slice** |
| Copy | ⧉ on fenced blocks copies plaintext (including `secret` fences) |
| Obfuscate | Context menu **.kb - Obfuscate** (selection required) → `⟦secret:base64⟧` (not encryption) |

### Topics and tickets

- **Topics** (`# TOPIC:`) organize subjects. Optional — no header (or `# TOPIC: other`) → topic **other**. In the edit-slice, **Cmd/Ctrl+Alt+T** opens a topic picker (type to filter); commit moves the subject under that topic. Empty topics are dropped when the last subject leaves them.
- **Refs:** `kb:registry/cleanup-images` or short `kb:proj-1234` (= `kb:other/proj-1234`).
- **Created date:** `- created: YYYY-MM-DD` is added automatically by **Append stub**; keep it when editing.
- **Git:** point `knowledge_base_file` at a path inside a git repo; `kb_git_friendly` writes mode `0644`. Keep secrets out of KB (or use obfuscate). Daily `notes_file` stays private/local chronologically; KB is the shareable runbook store.
- **Unify notes+KB?** Keep separate files: notes = dated journal + ticket log; KB = durable, searchable, git-friendly subjects. Linking via `kb:…` is the unification layer — merging into one file mixes ephemeral daily noise with curated runbooks.


- Hover is off while the KB file itself is focused
- Browse/Search preview reuses the open KB file view in the other pane (scroll only; does not steal the dropdown keyboard)
- Slugs are lowercase with hyphens (`My Topic` → `my-topic`)
- Colors follow your active UI / color scheme

## Safety

- HTTPS-only YouTrack / GitLab bases; private/loopback/CGNAT hosts rejected  
- Hover / navigate opens **https:// only** (rejects `javascript:` / `file:` / plain http)  
- API calls refuse HTTP redirects (Bearer / PRIVATE-TOKEN not forwarded)  
- UI / console errors scrub configured tokens plus `perm:` / `glpat-` / Authorization headers  
- API error dialogs omit full request URLs and raw response dumps  
- Notes read-modify-write serialized (`_notes_io_lock`); atomic write + mode `0600`  
- Notes file hard cap 8 MiB (read/write); `notes_path_jail` keeps the file under home by default  
- Package defaults ship **empty** tokens — put real tokens only in `Packages/User/ST4Notes.sublime-settings`  
- DONE / REVIEW YouTrack state changes require confirm (single-line only)

Do **not** minify / bytecode-obfuscate this package: Sublime loads plain `.py` from the package folder; shipping secrets-free source is the safety model.

## Getting started tab

After install (Package Control **or** a git symlink) Sublime opens a scratch tab
with the same text as `messages/install.txt` — the same mechanism LSP uses
(`messages.json` → `install`) plus `plugin_loaded` so symlink installs still
get a tab.

- Auto-show once (flag in Sublime's cache dir). Set `show_getting_started` to `false` to never auto-open.
- Re-open any time: **.notes - Hub → Getting started**
- Starter journal (only if missing/empty): `examples/ST4Notes.example` (KB seed is the **kb** package)

## Install / live symlink

Do **not** keep a second `notes_plugin.py` / `*.sublime-commands` / `*.sublime-syntax` under `Packages/User/` (even in a `_disabled_*` folder) — Sublime loads those and duplicates every Command Palette entry.

```bash
ln -s "/path/to/sublime-text-packages/notes" \
  "$HOME/Library/Application Support/Sublime Text/Packages/notes"
```

## Requirements

- Sublime Text 4 with **Python 3.14** plugin host (see `.python-version`; build ≥4169)
- Package folder name must be **`notes`** (Package Control name aligned; Settings menus use `${packages}/notes/…`; Command Palette prefix **`.notes`**)
- Optional YouTrack + GitLab tokens for API features
